  "body": "## What changed\n- replace rolling 24h/7d planning metrics with calendar windows in Europe/Warsaw:\n  - Today: 00:00 -> now\n  - Current week: Monday 00:00 -> now\n  - Previous full week: previous Monday 00:00 -> current Monday 00:00\n- calculate required bots from the previous full week once that whole window is covered\n- before a full previous week exists, estimate weekly volume from the average daily number of new listings observed since baseline, then scale to 7 days\n- expose whether Today / Current week are only partial because baseline started after the window began\n- keep baseline listings excluded from new-listing counts\n- replace the price-matrix columns with Today / Current week / Previous full week / Required bots\n- change the observer scheduler from the old 24h default to a 15-minute cooldown after a completed full pass\n- keep the collector single-threaded so long scans never overlap; effective start-to-start spacing is pass duration + cooldown\n- retain `FLIPBOT_MARKET_STATS_INTERVAL_HOURS` as a legacy fallback, while adding `FLIPBOT_MARKET_STATS_REFRESH_MINUTES`\n\n## Recommendation semantics\n- full previous week available -> exact previous-week listing count is the only input\n- no full previous week yet -> `ceil(observed_since_baseline / tracked_calendar_days * 7)`\n- one bot capacity remains 5 new conversations/day = 35/week\n\n## Tests\n- calendar Monday/midnight boundaries\n- weekly projection from partial baseline data\n- bot-capacity rounding\n- refresh cooldown defaults, bounds, explicit override, and legacy compatibility",
